apache2 (2.4.58-1ubuntu8.17) noble-security; urgency=medium

  * SECURITY UPDATE: Information disclosure in mod_dav_fs
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-58415.patch: Block dav state dir in
      modules/dav/fs/mod_dav_fs.c, ../repos.c, and ../repos.h
    - CVE-2026-58415
  * SECURITY UPDATE: Improper validation in mod_proxy_ftp
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-63045.patch: Check PASV addresses in
      modules/proxy/mod_proxy_ftp.c
    - CVE-2026-63045
  * SECURITY UPDATE: Buffer overflow in mod_vhost_alias
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-63292.patch: Harden vhost_alias in
      modules/mappers/mod_vhost_alias.c
    - CVE-2026-63292
  * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in mod_xml2enc
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-63686.patch: Handle incomplete input in
      modules/filters/mod_xml2enc.c
    - CVE-2026-63686
  * SECURITY UPDATE: Inconsistent interpretation of HTTP Requests
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-63718.patch: Drop hop-by-hop headers from
      UWSGI in modules/proxy/mod_proxy_uwsgi.c,
      test/modules/proxy/test_03_uwsgi.py, and
      test/modules/proxy/uwsgi_faker.py
    - CVE-2026-63718
  * SECURITY UPDATE: Authentication bypass and Use-after-free in
    mod_auth_digest
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-7363X.patch: Stop caching the configured realm
      during config processing and always call ap_auth_name(r) to determine
      the configured realm in modules/aaa/config.m4 and ../mod_auth_digest.c
    - CVE-2026-73636
    - CVE-2026-73637
  * SECURITY UPDATE: Path equivalence vulnerability in mod_userdir
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-79768.patch: Fix userdir check in
      modules/mappers/mod_userdir.c
    - CVE-2026-79768
  * SECURITY UPDATE: Integer overflow in mod_dav_fs
    - debian/patches/CVE-2026-93546.patch: Limit dav namespaces in
      modules/dav/fs/dbm.c and ../main/props.c
    - CVE-2026-93546
